# syntax: shell assignments only — no logic, no command substitution, no exports.
#
# The single source of truth for the media toolchain every ClipMux image and
# agent download consumes. Nothing else may hard-code a version, a URL or a
# digest — `build_ffmpeg.sh` refuses to build if a hash is blank, and
# `verify_toolchain.sh` compares the installed FFmpeg against FFMPEG_VERSION, so
# a drift here surfaces as a failed build rather than as a subtly different
# encoding of every job. Workers report these versions when they claim work, and
# the server skips a worker that cannot meet the output contract.
#
# Source it, do not execute it:
#   set -a; . toolchain/versions.env; set +a
#
# Why a source build at all: the distribution FFmpeg that used to be installed
# here (`apt-get install ffmpeg`) has `scale_cuda` without its `format` option —
# the option the NVIDIA scaling path passes to pin the surface format. That is a
# build-time property of FFmpeg's CUDA filters, so it can only be fixed by
# building them ourselves. See build_ffmpeg.sh for the exact configure line.

# ─── FFmpeg ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FFMPEG_VERSION=9.0.1
FFMPEG_SHA256=cf38e0e28c7e5605942c4a77755349b0145804a397af37eb1fb4c77cb237f635
FFMPEG_URL=https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-${FFMPEG_VERSION}.tar.xz

# ─── nv-codec-headers (ffnvcodec) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# FFmpeg 9.0.1's configure requires `ffnvcodec >= 12.1.14.0`; 12.1.14.0 is also
# the header release that documents a Linux driver floor of 530.41.03, which is
# the floor the whole CUDA path in this project inherits. The pinned commit is
# the tag's commit, so a moved or re-tagged release cannot change the bytes.
# `make install PREFIX=/usr` is deliberate: it drops `ffnvcodec.pc` where
# pkg-config already looks.
NV_CODEC_HEADERS_VERSION=n12.1.14.0
# The commit is *provenance*; the sha256 is the *integrity* check, and they are
# different values. GitHub's codeload tarball for a commit is not byte-stable
# across compression changes, so the hash below is verified on download and the
# commit is recorded in the build manifest; if GitHub ever re-packs the archive,
# the build fails loudly instead of silently building a different tree.
NV_CODEC_HEADERS_SHA=1889e62e2d35ff7aa9baca2bceb14f053785e6f1
NV_CODEC_HEADERS_SHA256=e30d4791fd386de8b5c9f88dec781e546ec148b8808440dd421da5f26c2700ae
NV_CODEC_HEADERS_URL=https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers/archive/${NV_CODEC_HEADERS_SHA}.tar.gz
NV_CODEC_HEADERS_GIT=https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers

# ─── Shaka Packager ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Checksum-pinned: a packager that silently changes version changes the bytes
# every job produces, which is not something to discover from a diff.
# docs/architecture.md requires >= 3.9.1: AES-128 for MP4 arrived in 3.8 and was
# fixed for CMAF in 3.9.1 (issue 1587). 3.9.3 is what clipmux-lms runs in
# production; it needs the init-segment workaround for Shaka issue 1616 (see
# clipmux-lms transcoding/hls/mp4.py) until a release fixes it. Re-run the
# Phase 1 player tests (hls.js, Safari, ExoPlayer) on every packager upgrade.
# Digests are the published release-asset SHA-256s.
SHAKA_VERSION=v3.9.3
SHAKA_RELEASE_URL=https://github.com/shaka-project/shaka-packager/releases/download/${SHAKA_VERSION}
SHAKA_LINUX_X64_SHA256=7a3cf35ad146fd7810b4ededab363c8a3e6121d1b2c8391f53863126186f9ee6
SHAKA_LINUX_ARM64_SHA256=d3a50cecc139b54435be1bbbfba5c0ea822d9e1e7edc3531f7821fba65ceebb0
SHAKA_OSX_X64_SHA256=64f0fece6a5f80603d9f19b3adc70e626303feb63b459fd599132632b8e76420
SHAKA_OSX_ARM64_SHA256=b3049e743451aab5c2cd7b1316a4ce055682c41effe06a49e2e6c95a9243d351
# The linux-x64 pair, recorded in the FFmpeg build manifest/NOTICE.
SHAKA_URL=${SHAKA_RELEASE_URL}/packager-linux-x64
SHAKA_SHA256=${SHAKA_LINUX_X64_SHA256}

# ─── whisper.cpp (speech to text, P5-T11) ────────────────────────────────────
# Built from source by build_whisper.sh, with the CPU backend in every x86-64
# variant ggml ships (picked at run time from what the CPU supports) and the
# Vulkan backend, which covers AMD, Intel and NVIDIA (with `graphics` in
# NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES) from one build. Pinned like nv-codec-headers: the
# commit is the tag's (provenance), the sha256 is the codeload tarball's
# (integrity). Built without libcurl, so the tool itself can't fetch anything.
WHISPER_CPP_VERSION=v1.9.5
WHISPER_CPP_SHA=d1be6fde11ac6e0407606b4e42fe72d34add8037
WHISPER_CPP_SHA256=645445da884df6dbd52b30f82d7be7c01d1767c938714e477e786b88d529e9f4
WHISPER_CPP_URL=https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp/archive/${WHISPER_CPP_SHA}.tar.gz

# ─── CUDA (whisper.cpp's CUDA backend, D131) ─────────────────────────────────
# amd64 images only. Modal runs gVisor, which passes CUDA through but not
# always the Vulkan ICD, so an NVIDIA serverless machine transcribed on its
# CPU; ggml's CUDA backend runs there. install_cuda.sh installs these exact
# toolkit packages from NVIDIA's apt repository for Ubuntu 24.04 (the keyring
# checked by sha256), build_whisper.sh builds against them and copies the
# runtime libraries (cudart, cuBLAS) beside whisper-cli, and the toolkit is
# purged again. The driver's own libcuda.so.1 is the container runtime's.
# Architectures: the GPUs NVENC providers rent, T4 (7.5), A10G and RTX
# A4000/A5000 (8.6), L4 and L40S (8.9), plus PTX for newer cards. CUDA 12.x
# runs on any driver from 525 (minor-version compatibility), below the 530
# NVENC already needs.
CUDA_VERSION=12.8
CUDA_REPO_URL=https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos/ubuntu2404/x86_64
CUDA_KEYRING_URL=${CUDA_REPO_URL}/cuda-keyring_1.1-1_all.deb
CUDA_KEYRING_SHA256=d2a6b11c096396d868758b86dab1823b25e14d70333f1dfa74da5ddaf6a06dba
CUDA_NVCC_VERSION=12.8.93-1
CUDA_CUDART_VERSION=12.8.90-1
CUDA_CCCL_VERSION=12.8.90-1
CUDA_DRIVER_DEV_VERSION=12.8.90-1
CUDA_CUBLAS_VERSION=12.8.5.5-1
WHISPER_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES="75-real;86-real;89"

# The speech models. The image bakes them in (D118: a serverless machine is
# new for every job, so a fetch at start downloaded them on every job); a PC
# agent fetches them by digest into its models directory (CLIPMUX_MODELS_DIR),
# never through the sandboxed tool.
# Hugging Face URLs are pinned to a repository commit; the sha256 is the LFS
# object's. large-v3-turbo is MIT-licensed (OpenAI); Silero VAD is MIT.
# q8_0 is P5-T11's measurement (D077): on 120 s of speech it was the fastest
# on a 6-core CPU (0.40 of real time) and on an RX 6600 XT over Vulkan
# (0.05), ahead of q5_0 (0.51, 0.09) and f16 (0.42, 0.18), with the same text.
WHISPER_MODEL_NAME=large-v3-turbo-q8_0
WHISPER_MODEL_URL=https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp/resolve/5359861c739e955e79d9a303bcbc70fb988958b1/ggml-large-v3-turbo-q8_0.bin
WHISPER_MODEL_SHA256=317eb69c11673c9de1e1f0d459b253999804ec71ac4c23c17ecf5fbe24e259a1
WHISPER_MODEL_SIZE=874188075
WHISPER_VAD_MODEL_NAME=silero-v6.2.0
WHISPER_VAD_MODEL_URL=https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/whisper-vad/resolve/9ffd54a1e1ee413ddf265af9913beaf518d1639b/ggml-silero-v6.2.0.bin
WHISPER_VAD_MODEL_SHA256=2aa269b785eeb53a82983a20501ddf7c1d9c48e33ab63a41391ac6c9f7fb6987
WHISPER_VAD_MODEL_SIZE=885098

# ─── Managed base images ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Modal/RunPod worker (Phase 4): Ubuntu 24.04 + CUDA 12.9 + cuDNN 9 (cuDNN is kept for
# future GPU captioning; the CUDA toolkit itself is *not* needed at build
# time because FFmpeg's CUDA filters are compiled with clang to PTX).
# The digest is the manifest-list digest, pinned so `nvidia/cuda:12.9.2-...`
# cannot be re-pushed under us.
CUDA_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:12.9.2-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu24.04
CUDA_BASE_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:070f8f2672df1b05b84c0409a5fd1d54ddfd646e5b9d8dee7878131271b563fc
CUDA_BASE_IMAGE_REF=${CUDA_BASE_IMAGE}@${CUDA_BASE_IMAGE_DIGEST}

# The clipmux image and the Linux agent build on Ubuntu 24.04.
AGENT_BASE_IMAGE=ubuntu:24.04
TARGET_UBUNTU_VERSION=24.04
TARGET_UBUNTU_CODENAME=noble
